    {
      "id": "ADB-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-adelic-box-coordinates",
      "title": "A common finite denominator and an archimedean lattice",
      "statement": "A compact family of vectors in (𝔸_F⊗_F E)^M lies in a coordinate box with one positive integer denominator N at all finite places and one archimedean ℓ¹ radius r>0. Within that denominator, the rational coordinate subgroup is (N⁻¹𝒪_F)^(2M), embedded in real dimension 2[F:ℚ]M.",
      "hypotheses": "F is totally real and E/F is CM quadratic. Fix an F-basis of E. The local integral lattices are taken in the chosen coefficient basis of the two-dimensional algebra over F_v. They are compact open, including at split places.",
      "correspondence": "The source treats tuples in the tensor-product coordinates, constructs the additive subgroup from all finite-place constraints, computes its archimedean norm and rank and bounds rational intersections with compact sets.",
      "dependencies": [],
      "equations": [
        "lifts-adelic-box-factors"
      ],
