    {
      "id": "ADB-03",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-adelic-box-count",
      "title": "A uniform cutoff and growth bound for the dilated rational count",
      "statement": "For compact Ω and the scalar flow, the count of nonzero X∈E^M with τ(−x)X∈Ω vanishes for x<x₀ and is at most C exp(2[F:ℚ]M x) for x≥x₀. For Ω⊂B_N(r) one can choose x₀=log(r₀/r), C=(5r/r₀)^ν whenever the positive radius r₀≤1 gives P_N(r₀)=1.",
      "hypotheses": "The scalar flow acts by exp(x) at the real places and by one at finite places. The radius r₀ is strictly below all positive real sizes in B_N(1), unless that set of nonzero vectors is empty. In the isotropic shell application the compact set is an image under the Hermitian pairing and M=1 in this counting theorem.",
      "correspondence": "The source uses finiteness of rational tuples in a compact box to choose r₀. The additional choice min(1,d/(2N)) follows directly from the field norm of any nonzero integral coordinate. Equality at the threshold lies in the upper-bound branch. The Gaussian example verifies the cutoff and the first closed shell.",
      "dependencies": [
        "ADB-01",
        "ADB-02"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "lifts-adelic-box-flow-bound"
      ],
